 34SI c  {+34}Al in 1+ isomeric state produced through the |b decay of          
 34SI2c  {+34}Mg.  {+34}Mg produced through fragmentation of 1.4 GeV proton     
 34SI3c  beam on a UC{-x} target at ISOLDE-CERN facility, selectively ionized   
 34SI4c  using the Resonance Ionization Laser Ion Source (RILIS) and selected   
 34SI5c  by the ISOLDE General Purpose Separator (GPS).  Nuclei were implanted  
 34SI6c  on a movable tape. Measured E|g, I|g, |g|g, |b|g, |g(t) using five     
 34SI7c  HPGe Clover detectors and a 3 cm thick NE102 plastic scintillator.     
